.. highlight:: none

.. _syn-tools-service-v3prepare:

service.v3prepare
=================

The Synapse ``service.v3prepare`` tool checks a Synapse service for readiness to upgrade to Synapse 3.x and, if the
check has no errors, prepares it. It runs the same check and preparation as the :ref:`storm-v3-prepare` Storm
command, for one service, and exits with a non-zero status when the service is not ready. Use ``--dry-run`` to only
check the service, without preparing it or recording anything. Run it against the leader of the service.

Syntax
------

``service.v3prepare`` is executed using ``python -m synapse.tools.service.v3prepare``. The command usage is as
follows:

.. shell:: --fail-ok python -m synapse.tools.service.v3prepare -h
